      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paseo_de_la_Castellana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The avenue cuts Madrid from south to north, described as the city's true structuring axis.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paseo_de_la_Castellana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The stretch north of the crossroads with Raimundo Fernández Villaverde was once named Avenida del Generalísimo during Franco's dictatorship.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paseo_de_la_Castellana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Along Castellana, the Santiago Bernabéu Stadium stands as a global football landmark and Real Madrid's home.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
